7-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Walls guarded the salt of Solnitsata, near Provadia, a town believed to have supplied salt throughout the Balkans, until an earthquake, it is believed, destroyed it."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-check-v-002 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Solnitsata was walled, the walls guarding its salt [S3]; Solnitsata lay near Provadia [S1]; Solnitsata was a town [S1]; the town is believed to have supplied salt throughout the Balkans [S4]; the town is believed to have been destroyed by an earthquake (hedge kept) [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-verify2-004 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Solnitsata is a prehistoric town (settlement) near Provadia, Bulgaria [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solnitsata]; Salt was produced at Solnitsata (it was a salt production site) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solnitsata]; Walls guarded the salt of Solnitsata (the settlement was walled to protect the salt) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solnitsata]; The town is believed to have supplied salt throughout the Balkans [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solnitsata]; The town is believed to have been destroyed by an earthquake [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solnitsata]"}]'::jsonb),
